# Copy this file to .env and adjust for your machine.

# Directory in which `make playground` scaffolds a throwaway project
# (via `djangorocket init`) for manual, local testing.
PLAYGROUND_BASE_DIR=/path/to/your/playground/dir

# The djangorocket checkout `make playground` installs into the playground's
# virtualenv in editable mode, so the `djangorocket` command run from inside the
# playground is that source. Defaults to the checkout you run `make` in; set it
# to develop against a different working tree.
# DJANGOROCKET_SRC_DIR=/path/to/another/djangorocket

# Interpreter used to build the playground project's virtualenv. Defaults to
# the `python3` on PATH, matching the generated project's `make bootstrap`.
# PLAYGROUND_PYTHON=python3.13

# `make playground` also points the `djangorocket` command on PATH at the
# checkout (a pipx editable install), so the bare command typed inside a
# playground is the local build with nothing to activate. Set this to 0 to link
# only the playground's own virtualenv and leave the global command alone.
# PLAYGROUND_LINK_CLI=0
